> >> Are you new to NetHack? If so, do you want some pointers?

> >> archmage84

> > Yes, I've only been playing a week or so.

> > Some pointers would be helpful. :)

> 1. Depending on your class don't decend until you gain at *least* one
> level. If you're a "non-fighter" such as a wizard, wait 2 for every level
> down. In other words, you shouldn't be on level 2 until experience level 3
> and level 3 until experience level 4.

I think opinions about this vary.  Don't descend too fast, and
don't descend too slowly, but the definitions of too fast and
too slowly are rather vague.  I generally try not to be more
than one level deeper than my experience (but I once reached
minetown at XL1).  And I tend to level fighters up more quickly
than other classes (probably because it's a lot easier).

Also, these rules may be weakened if you encounter some good
armor, earlier.

> 2. When you find a down staircase ">", go down it and then immediately up
> it again. That way if you fall down a trap door, you know how to get back
> to the other level.

You also get the resident monsters generated at the level you
have when you go down the first time, which is possibly lower
than the one you have when you go down to actually fight them.

    [...]
> 4. Until you get up to about 100 spell points, don't worry about what sort
> of armor you're wearing, you want to get your AC low as quickly as you can
> (without becoming burdened) so you don't die from attacks.

It's not just a question of spell points.  Up to about level 10,
and AC of -5 is generally sufficient.  If you get there without
metal body armor, there's no problem spell casting.  But AC
before spell casting ability, at least up to a point.

> 5. You don't have to kill every monster. If you start losing, making a
> quick getaway, particularly from more than one monster is always better.

Engrave Elbereth, and let your pet do the dirty work.

    [...]
> 8. use one good weapon - wizards for example get a quarterstaff which is
> easily good enough to last you to level 15.

A wizard should be using daggers, mostly.

More generally, get some sort of ranged weapon.  Almost as
important as lowering AC.

> 9. Eventually you will find two down staircases on one level (before or at
> level 5) One of them decends to yet another similar level, but the other
> will decend to an open area with strangely shaped walls and no real rooms.
> Wait until you have a) a negative AC b) are skilled in a decent weapon and
> c) have at lest 50 hit points before you explore it.

My rule there: wait until my pet is no longer "little".  That's
enough for him to take care of most of the denizons.  And most
of the time, it's the mines which provide the good armor.

